  /// <summary>
  /// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  /// Invitation — an administrator invites a person into a tenant (and project)
  /// with a set of roles. The invitee opens the link, proves the invitation's
  /// channel and gets an ACTIVE account with that channel already verified:
  ///
  /// * SMS / EMAIL: a one-time code is sent to `address` (StartInvitationAcceptance)
  ///   and AcceptInvitation checks it; the phone or email is then verified.
  /// * OIDC: the invitee signs in with the tenant's identity provider
  ///   `idp_provider_id`; the external identity is linked to the new account.
  /// * PASSKEY: the invitee registers a passkey during acceptance.
  ///
  /// The link carries a random accept token; only its keyed hash is stored, and
  /// ResendInvitation replaces it (the previous link stops working). Roles are
  /// role CODES bound in the invitation's tenant when it is accepted; reserved
  /// platform roles are refused, and `organization_owner` needs an inviter who
  /// holds it (or a cross-tenant admin). Rows are isolated by tenant.
  /// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  /// </summary>
